>> IKE-6.29
TEST_DESCRIPTION
IKE MUST not respond to an incoming packet with two Transforms if
the Next Payload field  of first Transform is not 3, or the Next 
Payload field of the second Transform is not 0.
Main mode/ANVL initiated/Negative
TEST_REFERENCE
NEGATIVE: RFC 2408 s3.6 p30 Transform Payload
          RFC 2409 s5.4 p16 Phase 1 Authenticated With a
          Pre-Shared Key
TEST_METHOD
- ANVL: Send <HDR,SA> Packet with one Proposal and two Transforms with
        Next Payload field of first Transform to <NP1> and that of
        second Transform to <NP2>
-  DUT: Do not send <HDR,SA> packet
- CASE: <NP1> = 0, <NP2> = 0
- CASE: <NP1> = 1, <NP2> = 1
- CASE: <NP1> = 3, <NP2> = 2
TEST_CLASSIFICATION
MUST
