A Protocol implementation SHOULD continue to support incoming
traffic on the old SA until traffic is received under the protection 
of the new SA.
Quick mode/DUT initiated/Positive
TEST_REFERENCE
RFC 2408 s4.3 p51 Security Association Modification
RFC 2409 s5.5 p19 Phase 2 - Quick Mode
TEST_METHOD
- ANVL: Establish one ISAKMP SA with DUT
- ANVL: Externally cause DUT to initiate an IPSEC SA
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(1),SA1,Ni,KE>
- ANVL: Send <HDR*,HASH(2),SA1,Nr,KE>
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(3)>
- ANVL: Externally cause DUT to initiate an another IPSEC SA
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(1),SA2,Ni,KE>
- ANVL: Send <HDR*,HASH(2),SA2,Nr,KE>
-  DUT: Send <HDR*,HASH(3)>
- ANVL: Send secured ICMP Echo-request using SA1
-  DUT: Forward the ICMP Echo-request to Local Host
TEST_CLASSIFICATION
SHOULD
