<< IKE-13.1: Passed

>> IKE-23.1
TEST_DESCRIPTION
It is observed in some IKE daemon, that on receipt of an INVALID-SPI
notification, they delete the IPsec SA referred to by the SPI
contained in the notification data and all "associated" IPsec SAs,
if the ISAKMP message originates from the right IP address
(An attacker can easily learn the SPI of IPsec SA and inject the
informational packets to the network. It is to check if DUT is robust
enough to detect that)
TEST_REFERENCE
Web ref: http://securityfocus.com/archive/1/348637
RFC 2408 s5.5 p63 Proposal Payload Processing
TEST_METHOD
- ANVL: Establish an ISAKMP SA with DUT
- ANVL: Establish an IPSec SA with DUT
- ANVL: Send an secured ICMP Echo Request from Remote Host
-  DUT: Forward the ICMP Echo Request to Local Host
- ANVL: As an attacker sniff the forwarded encrypted ICMP Echo
        Request. Take out the SPI from the encrypted packet as
        it is not encrypted and note down the SPI
- ANVL: As an attacker send <HDR, NOT> Packet with notify message
        INVALID-SPI
-  DUT: Do not delete the IPSec SA as the notification is not
        encrypted using the established ISAKMP SA
- ANVL: Send an secured ICMP Echo Request from Remote Host
-  DUT: Forward the ICMP Echo Request to Local Host
TEST_CLASSIFICATION
MUST
TEST_TOPOLOGY
TOPOLOGY-0

